Assembler Version 15
====================
Assembled by: version 14 (asm and debug build both assembled by v14)

Build notes: This version produces both a normal build (asm.out) and a
debug build (asm_debug.out) using define:enable_debug. The debug build
is used to assemble version 16.

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 14, plus macros, shift operators, and label
scope management:

Syntax:
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax (LDA, STA, etc.)
- All addressing modes (immediate, zero page, absolute, indexed, indirect)
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- .data directive for byte/string data
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Character literals: 'x', '\n', '\\', '\''
- Expression evaluation with +, -, <<, >> operators (left-to-right)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- Optional colon after label definitions (label: as well as label)
- Local labels with . prefix
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly with forward reference tracking
- Automatic zero page vs absolute addressing

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file
- .zeropage - switch to zero page section
- .code - switch to code section
- .data - declare raw byte data
- .ifdef label - begin conditional block if label is defined
- .endif - end conditional block
- .macro NAME [param1 param2 ...] - begin macro definition (new)
- .endmacro - end macro definition (new)

Command line:
- Variable argument count (2 or more arguments)
- define:label - pre-define a label with value $0001

Macro system:
- Macro definitions stored on heap with body text and parameter names
- Invocation by macro name (parsed like instructions)
- Text substitution of parameters during expansion
- Local labels (.label) scoped per invocation via EXPANSION_ID
- Recursion detection by walking scope stack
- Memory source reading for macro body expansion
- File stack used to push macro expansion as memory source

Label scope:
- Label scope stack (label_scope.asm) for macro expansions
- SCOPE_STACK at $0400 (256 bytes, 5-byte entries)
- EXPANSION_ID16 provides synthetic scope pointer for local labels
- push_label_scope / pop_label_scope / init_scope_stack / reset_scope_stack
- Scope stack bounds check (err_macro_nesting_too_deep)

Error handling: same as version 14, plus:
- err_expected_shift ($1A): Expected << or >>
- err_macro_name_expected ($1B): .macro without name
- err_macro_shadows_instruction ($1C): Macro name conflicts with instruction
- err_duplicate_macro ($1D): Duplicate macro definition
- err_endmacro_without_macro: .endmacro outside macro definition
- err_unclosed_macro: Missing .endmacro at end of file
- err_recursive_macro: Recursive macro invocation detected
- err_too_few_arguments: Not enough arguments for macro
- err_too_many_arguments: Too many arguments for macro
- err_macro_nesting_too_deep: Scope stack overflow
- Include traceback shows file inclusion chain on errors
- err_fwdref_tracking now conditional (debug build only)

New in this version (relative to version 14):
- << and >> shift operators in expressions
  - parse_term_with_selector for shift count parsing
  - Added <, >, :, = as token terminators in compare_end_of_token
- .macro/.endmacro directive support
  - capture_macro_line captures macro body to heap during definition
  - IN_MACRO_DEF flag tracks macro capture state
  - MACRO_DEF_PTR_L/H points to heap during capture
  - Macro bodies stored on heap with null-terminated parameter list
- Macro expansion via expand_macro
  - MACRO_ARG_BUF at $0500 for argument text during expansion
  - push_memory_source pushes macro body onto file stack
  - Parameter substitution during read_char from memory source
  - MACRO_ENTRY_L/H for recursion detection
- Label scope stack (new label_scope.asm module)
  - SCOPE_STACK at $0400, 5-byte entries
  - Synthetic EXPANSION_ID for local label scoping in macros
  - FS_POP_MEMORY_HOOK = pop_label_scope for automatic cleanup
  - Bounds check against SCOPE_LIMIT
- Optional colon after label definitions (label:)
- NEXT_CHAR variable for single-character lookahead
- CURR_OUT_FILE for output file handle (used by error handler)
- read_char aliased to file_stack_read_char
- Error handler shows include/expansion traceback
- IFDEF_DECISIONS moved to $0800 (separate from zero page)
- IFDEF_INDEX moved to $08FF (non-zero-page, separate byte)

